bug_report:
Address sanitizer is not compatible with named address spaces
From [1], gcc is doing a KASAN check on a percpu address (when percpu access is implemented using named address spaces). This is not a "real" address, just an offset from the segment register.

The testcase

--cut here--
int __seg_gs m;

int foo (void)
{
  return m;
}
--cut here--

does not show any special handling that would handle segment registers.

